+## Rotating the password
+
+To change the `password` without signing users out, pass a list: put the new password first and keep the old one after it.
+
+```js
+const session = await useSession(event, {
+  password: [process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD, process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_OLD],
+});
+```
+
+The first password seals every session, and every password in the list can open one. A session cookie sealed with the old password is opened and then resealed with the new one on the same request, so active users migrate on their own. A session carried by the session header is opened, but cannot be resealed.
+
+Each password must be at least 32 characters, and the list cannot be empty. Every extra password costs one more PBKDF2 derivation when a cookie does not open (a forged one, for example), so keep the list short. Remove the old password once the rotation window has passed, because until then it can still open sessions.
+
 ## Get Data from a Session
 
 To get data from a session, we will still use `useSession`. Under the hood, it will use `getSession` to get the session.
